
  FSL red team box.

  Everything HTTP leaves through the stamping proxy, so the address an alert
  carries is the proxy's, not this box's. Raw TCP - nmap, nc - does not go
  through it and leaves from here. The red window prints both, and which one
  a labelled window is scored against depends on which you use.

    target       echo $FSL_TARGET      # the site, not the appliance
    recon        nmap -sV -p 8080 $FSL_TARGET_HOST
                 whatweb $FSL_TARGET
    discovery    ffuf -u $FSL_TARGET/FUZZ -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt
                 gobuster dir -u $FSL_TARGET -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt
    scanning     nikto -h $FSL_TARGET
    exploitation sqlmap -u "$FSL_TARGET/rest/products/search?q=1" --batch

  Name a window in the red console before you start, and stop it when you are
  done: everything sent in between is attributed to that name and scored.

